{
 "item": "24",
 "title": "Decaying 2-D turbulence: vorticity, E(t) and the enstrophy Z(t), spectra and their ratio",
 "status": "final",
 "caption": "Decaying two-dimensional turbulence in the doubly periodic box [0, 2 pi)^2: 2050^2 particles (h = 5 dx), initial energy spectrum E(k) ~ k^4 exp(-2 (k / k0)^2) with k0 = 10 and random phases (fixed seed), u' = 1, Ma 0.02 on the initial peak speed; the Newtonian fluid of viscosity mu + kappa / 2 = 1e-3 (Re = u' / (k0 nu) = 100) and the micropolar fluid K = 3, j = l^2, l = 1/7 (|k| l = 1 at k = 7) with the same far-field viscosity, both from the same field (w = omega / 2). Z is the enstrophy (1/2) <omega^2> = sum k^2 E(k). (a, b) Vorticity of the Newtonian and the micropolar run at t = 2 and (c) their difference (the repeats of the two runs on one card, which carry the snapshots at t >= 2; deposit on a 1024^2 grid, shown at 512^2; the difference low-passed with exp(-(k / 100)^2) against the grid-scale noise of the deposit). (d) E and Z of the micropolar runs (j = l^2, and j = l^2 / 100 with the same dt) against the Newtonian run (thick: E, thin: Z), with the shifted-lattice floor and the Newtonian run at 1025^2 (resolution); the repeats on one card and the Newtonian run on the other card lie on the shifted-lattice floor (Section 18.5). (e) Energy spectra at t = 1 and 4 (paler = later) with the 1025^2 run at t = 4. (f) The ratio of the spectra micropolar / Newtonian at t = 2 in bins of about 8 % in k (solid: j = l^2, dash-dotted: j = l^2 / 100) with the floor |ratio - 1| of the shifted-lattice run (shaded), and the linear estimates for a single Fourier mode decaying alone at the slow rate of the two-mode system with j = l^2 (dashed) and at the quasi-steady mu_eff (j -> 0, dotted).",
